# healthcare-iac-status — quick reference
#
# This example shows how to call the composite action that gates your
# pipeline on healthcare-iac's view of your contract. The action returns
# `status: ready | provisioning | partial | blocked | unknown`. Treat
# anything other than `ready` as a hard fail (the canonical workflow in
# `build-and-promote.yml` does exactly this in the `status` job).
#
# Full action reference: .github/actions/healthcare-iac-status/action.yml

- name: Check healthcare-iac status (dev)
  uses: TheSmallCompany/healthcare-iac-onboarding/.github/actions/healthcare-iac-status@main
  with:
    customer-code: "{{ .CustomerCode }}"
    contract-path: "infra-contract.yaml" # path INSIDE your repo
    environment: "dev"
    # Env-scoped variable: the job must declare `environment: <env>` so
    # `vars.AWS_ROLE_ARN` resolves to that environment's role.
    aws-role-arn: ${{ vars.AWS_ROLE_ARN }}
    aws-region: us-east-1

# Outputs:
#   status        — ready | provisioning | partial | blocked | unknown
#   sleep-state   — awake | light-sleep | deep-sleep | unknown
#   contract-version
#   provisioned-count
#   pending-count
#   blocking-issues  — JSON array of GitHub issue URLs
#   details          — full JSON for diagnostics

# Common patterns
# ───────────────
#
# 1. Hard-fail when not ready (canonical):
#
#    - name: Fail closed if not ready
#      if: steps.status.outputs.status != 'ready'
#      run: |
#        echo "::error::status=${{ steps.status.outputs.status }}"
#        echo "Blocking: ${{ steps.status.outputs.blocking-issues }}"
#        exit 1
#
# 2. Skip the build (instead of fail) when sleep-state isn't awake.
#    Useful for nightly cron jobs that shouldn't fire during deep-sleep:
#
#    - name: Skip when sleeping
#      if: steps.status.outputs.sleep-state != 'awake'
#      run: |
#        echo "::notice::infrastructure is ${{ steps.status.outputs.sleep-state }}; skipping"
#        exit 0
#
# 3. Check status for the target environment. Set `environment: "<env>"`
#    on the job AND pass `${{ vars.AWS_ROLE_ARN }}` (the bot writes this
#    env-scoped variable to each GitHub Environment on /bind) — the role
#    is resolved per environment automatically. No suffix-by-string
#    switching needed.
